Subject: [PATCH] log: a configuration payload reaches the log with its secrets redacted

46 log lines (the data model's decoders, the controller's analyze_* handlers, the dev-test
encoder) printed whole subdocs, mostly on parse failures; SetPolicy's event and the AP and client
capability decoders on every call. The SSID subdocs carry each network's PassPhrase, so a
malformed SetSSID wrote the passphrases into the controller's log, which the platform's log
tarballs and log upload can carry off the box.

util::loggable_payload() gives what a log may print: JSON with the value of every key whose name
holds pass, key, psk, secret or credential (any case, any depth) replaced by "<redacted>"; a
buffer that does not parse, by its length only; NULL as "<none>". The 46 lines print that.
Tests (test_l1_util.cpp): a SetSSID payload's passphrases gone and its SSIDs kept; secrets under
other names and depths, a whole secret object included; a non-JSON buffer and NULL.
---
diff --git a/inc/util.h b/inc/util.h
index 485aecdb..361420a5 100644
--- a/inc/util.h
+++ b/inc/util.h
@@ -355,6 +355,20 @@ namespace util {
 	 */
 	bool set_net_uint16_from_host(const uint16_t host_val, void* const ptr);
 
+	/**
+	 * @brief A configuration payload (a subdoc's JSON) as it may go to a log.
+	 *
+	 * JSON comes back with the value of every secret-bearing key replaced by "<redacted>": a key
+	 * whose name holds "pass", "key", "psk", "secret" or "credential", in any case (PassPhrase,
+	 * Password, Key, PreSharedKey, ...), at any depth. Anything that does not parse as JSON comes
+	 * back as its length only, "<N bytes, not JSON>", since what it holds can't be told apart;
+	 * NULL as "<none>".
+	 *
+	 * @param payload The payload, a NUL-terminated string
+	 * @return std::string What a log may print
+	 */
+	std::string loggable_payload(const char *payload);
+
 } // namespace util
 
 #define __FILENAME__ (strrchr(__FILE__, '/') ? strrchr(__FILE__, '/') + 1 : __FILE__)
